  "id": "DrugBank_DB00461 - MONDO_6816",
  "verbalization": "Nabumetone, a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID), is associated with arthropathy through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Nabumetone may contribute to arthropathy via its role in inducing osteoarthritis, which in turn is linked to histamine and arthropathy. Additionally, Nabumetone is indicated for osteoarthritis, which is also associated with choline magnesium trisalicylate and arthropathy. These pathways highlight a potential link between NSAID use and arthropathy through inflammatory or metabolic mechanisms. The integration of these pathways implies that Nabumetone may influence arthropathy through a chain of indications that involve inflammatory mediators and metabolic processes. The evidence supports a mechanistic connection between Nabumetone and arthropathy, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
